    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0325" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg305"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1093.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 19, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 2d of Sep tember, transmitting a copy of a note of the 20th of
                    July last, addressed to you by our consul at Cape Town, communicating the facts
                    in regard to the non-restoration of the Tuscaloosa to her rightful owners. It
                    seems necessary to inform her Britannic Majesty’s government that this
                    government is unable to acquiesce in the disposition of the subject which that
                    government has made.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
